; Regression test for reading the journal again in a session, found while
; fixing #3253.
; https://github.com/ledger/ledger/issues/3253
;
; An interactive or --script session keeps its journal from command to
; command, and reads it again for reload and source.  Reading it again used
; to start from what the last reading left behind, where a fresh process
; starts clean:
;
; - the price history kept the prices the old journal recorded, so after
;   source a journal of other prices, pricedb showed the old journal's too;
; - the year a year directive set stayed set, so a transaction with no
;   year, before the directive, was dated in the directive's year (and the
;   default commodity of a D directive stayed set likewise, which
;   test/regress/3253.py covers);
; - a define like the one below was compiled in the scope of the command
;   that read the journal, and then evaluated after that command's report
;   was freed, a use after free;
; - a journal read from standard input came back empty.
;
; The script prints mytoday, the Food register and the prices; reads the
; journal again (reload) and prints them again; then reads another
; journal (source) and prints its prices.  --now fixes the year that the
; undated transaction falls in, before the year directive.

define mytoday = today

07/04 Undated
    Expenses:Food                         $5.00
    Assets:Cash

year 2020

2021/12/31 Opening
    Assets:Broker                         1 AGGY
    Equity:Opening Balances

2021/12/31=2022/01/04 Later
    Assets:Broker                         1 AGGY @@ $2.00
    Assets:Cash

P 2022/01/01 ZZZ $2
P 2022/01/03 ZZZ 3 EUR

test --now 2026/01/15 --script test/regress/3253_reload.dat
2026/01/15
25-Jul-04 Undated               Expenses:Food                 $5.00        $5.00
P 2021/12/31 00:00:00 AGGY $2.00
P 2022/01/01 00:00:00 ZZZ $2.00
P 2022/01/03 00:00:00 ZZZ EUR3
2026/01/15
25-Jul-04 Undated               Expenses:Food                 $5.00        $5.00
P 2021/12/31 00:00:00 AGGY $2.00
P 2022/01/01 00:00:00 ZZZ $2.00
P 2022/01/03 00:00:00 ZZZ EUR3
P 2020/01/01 00:00:00 XYZ $9.00
end test

; The same, with the journal read from standard input.

test -f - --now 2026/01/15 --script test/regress/3253_reload.dat
2026/01/15
25-Jul-04 Undated               Expenses:Food                 $5.00        $5.00
P 2021/12/31 00:00:00 AGGY $2.00
P 2022/01/01 00:00:00 ZZZ $2.00
P 2022/01/03 00:00:00 ZZZ EUR3
2026/01/15
25-Jul-04 Undated               Expenses:Food                 $5.00        $5.00
P 2021/12/31 00:00:00 AGGY $2.00
P 2022/01/01 00:00:00 ZZZ $2.00
P 2022/01/03 00:00:00 ZZZ EUR3
P 2020/01/01 00:00:00 XYZ $9.00
end test

; mytoday is today's date in the scope it was compiled in.  Compiled anew by
; a reload given its own --now, it must still be the session's date, not
; that of the reload's report: once freed, that report's memory went to the
; next command's, and mytoday took that command's --now.

test --now 2026/01/15 --script test/regress/3253_define.dat
2026/01/15
2026/01/15
end test
